kernel/backend/kernel/auth/data/common-passwords.txt.gz
  The bundled common-password list (SPEC.md 14.2), built with
  tools/build_common_passwords.py from the four lists below, in this order,
  keeping only entries of 12 characters or more, casefolded and
  deduplicated, less the lines the owner's brand check flags. The tool's
  docstring has the exact steps; rebuilt that way, the bytes are identical.

  The first three are taken from SecLists, a collection, at commit
  dbfb830d95e4f3da4fb7d7d277ed597de0ed7a18 (2026-11-12), folder
  Passwords/Common-Credentials/. https://github.com/danielmiessler/SecLists
  SecLists is MIT licensed, Copyright (c) 2018 Daniel Miessler
  (licenses/SecLists-MIT.txt). Each list keeps its own terms:

  1. 100k-most-used-passwords-NCSC.txt (git blob 38eb377), the UK National
     Cyber Security Centre's list of the 100,000 passwords most seen in
     breaches. Contains public sector information licensed under the Open
     Government Licence v3.0:
     https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/

  2. xato-net-10-million-passwords-1000000.txt (git blob e5e7323), the most
     common million of the ten million passwords Mark Burnett published in
     2015 (xato.net) and released into the public domain.

